  "claim_boundary": "This development-only protocol consumes the already-observed source-v4 public plan, unqualified development reader, theta0 v2, and transductive opportunity scan. It keeps all 112 synthetic roots and runs only decision indices 0-7 under the natural APPLY_CANDIDATE executor. Each root appends its four public onboarding experiences exactly once. Decision zero of every root must match the upstream scanner's complete 23-field frozen projection item by item before that root's selected branch is opened. For decisions one through seven, the exact prior post-settlement owner persistence is the next preaction input. Every preaction is appended to one create-only trace and fsynced before the source owner opens the selected actual-action branch; only then are reaction/outcome, owner writeback, social PE, and credit derived. Credit is never applied online and the cold gate remains 0/0/0. PASS only authorizes freezing a separate forced common-collection batch protocol. It does not authorize that protocol's execution, the forty-decision evaluation, any arm or effect estimate, reader qualification, formal or unseen evidence, Appendable, Readable, Learnable, Steerable, four-able completion, human evidence, or production ACTIVE. The sealed evaluator is loaded once after the global first fsynced preaction and retained behind the environment facade; it is never passed to the public forecast, reader, gate, or executor. Therefore the runtime-order claim is a cooperative development evidence boundary, not an OS security boundary."
